user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 53,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_uses_hedging_language",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text (post body): 1 if it contains hedging or qualifying language about its own claims, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the argument column only (OP's post body; may include later edits, which are not separated out; do not infer an initial version). Return 1 if the OP in their own voice uses at least one hedging or qualifying expression that softens or limits their own claim (e.g., 'I think maybe', 'might', 'perhaps', 'in some cases', 'generally', 'mostly', 'to my knowledge', 'I could be wrong', 'it seems'). Exclude hedges inside quoted text from others, quoted opponents, and edit notes/moderator notices not stating the OP's stance. Do not count purely generic 'I think/I believe' framing as a hedge unless it expresses uncertainty or limits scope. Return 0 if the argument is readable and contains no such hedging. Return null if argument is missing, empty, or unparseable."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 70,
    "feature": {
      "name": "op_explicit_hedging_or_self_doubt",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OP's own argument text (not quoted others, not marked edits): 1 if it contains explicit hedging or self-doubt markers about the OP's own view, else 0",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read only the argument column (OP post body). Return 1 if the OP, in their own voice, explicitly hedges or expresses doubt about their own view or claims, e.g. 'I might be wrong', 'I'm not sure', 'maybe', 'I could be missing something', 'to my knowledge', 'I'm unsure'. Ignore text in quotation of others, quoted opponents' positions, and edit sections (EDIT/marked edits). Generic politeness, rhetorical questions, or hedges unrelated to the OP's own stance (e.g. hedged statements about third parties' facts) do not count. Return 0 if the argument is assessable and has no such marker. Return null if argument is missing or unparseable. Do not use title, comments or conversation."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
